@host = https://localhost:5001
@tenantId = default

# NCode.Identity.OpenId management API — collection (list) endpoints.
#
# Pagination is keyset/cursor-based: pass '?limit=' to size the page (clamped to 100) and the
# previous response's 'continuationToken' back as '?cursor=' to fetch the next page. A null
# 'continuationToken' means there are no more pages.
#
# Authorization: every build enforces authentication. These require a GlobalAdmin token
# (servers, tenants) or a GlobalAdmin/TenantAdmin token for the request's tenant (clients).
# Obtain one by exchanging the configuration-seeded bootstrap administrator credential at the
# token endpoint (see ADR-0044).
#
# First-run bootstrap: the OpenID server and the static-single tenant are provisioned LAZILY by the
# OpenID runtime on first resolution, not at startup and not by these management endpoints (the list
# endpoints only read the store). On a fresh database 'GET /api/servers' and 'GET /api/tenants'
# therefore return empty until something resolves them. Invoke the discovery endpoint below once to
# build an OpenIdContext, which materializes the server (DefaultOpenIdServerFactory) and the tenant
# (StaticSingleTenantStrategy); after that they appear in the corresponding list endpoints.

### Discovery — materializes the server + static-single tenant on first call (run this before the lists)
GET {{host}}/.well-known/openid-configuration
Accept: application/json

### List clients (first page) — scoped to the addressed tenant
GET {{host}}/api/tenants/{{tenantId}}/clients?limit=50
Accept: application/json

### List clients (next page) — replace the cursor with the previous response's continuationToken
GET {{host}}/api/tenants/{{tenantId}}/clients?limit=50&cursor=REPLACE_WITH_continuationToken
Accept: application/json

### List servers (central-admin)
GET {{host}}/api/servers?limit=50
Accept: application/json

### List tenants (central-admin)
GET {{host}}/api/tenants?limit=50
Accept: application/json

### List resource servers (APIs) — scoped to the addressed tenant
GET {{host}}/api/tenants/{{tenantId}}/resource-servers?limit=50
Accept: application/json

### Create a resource server (API)
POST {{host}}/api/tenants/{{tenantId}}/resource-servers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "identifier": "https://api.example.com",
  "name": "Example API",
  "isDisabled": false,
  "settings": {}
}

### Get a resource server by its opaque id
GET {{host}}/api/tenants/{{tenantId}}/resource-servers/REPLACE_WITH_ResourceServerId
Accept: application/json

### Add a scope (permission) to a resource server
POST {{host}}/api/tenants/{{tenantId}}/resource-servers/REPLACE_WITH_ResourceServerId/scopes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "value": "read:messages",
  "description": "Read your messages."
}

### List a resource server's scopes
GET {{host}}/api/tenants/{{tenantId}}/resource-servers/REPLACE_WITH_ResourceServerId/scopes
Accept: application/json

### Delete a resource server (409 when it is a system resource server or still has client grants)
DELETE {{host}}/api/tenants/{{tenantId}}/resource-servers/REPLACE_WITH_ResourceServerId

### List a client's grants (its authorizations to resource servers) — first page
GET {{host}}/api/tenants/{{tenantId}}/clients/REPLACE_WITH_ClientId/grants?limit=50
Accept: application/json

### Grant a client access to a resource server with a subset of its scopes (422 when a scope is not defined on the API)
POST {{host}}/api/tenants/{{tenantId}}/clients/REPLACE_WITH_ClientId/grants
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "resourceServerId": "REPLACE_WITH_ResourceServerId",
  "scopes": ["read:messages"]
}

### Get a client's grant to a specific resource server
GET {{host}}/api/tenants/{{tenantId}}/clients/REPLACE_WITH_ClientId/grants/REPLACE_WITH_ResourceServerId
Accept: application/json

### Replace the granted scopes for a client's grant (422 when a scope is not defined on the API) — returns 204
PUT {{host}}/api/tenants/{{tenantId}}/clients/REPLACE_WITH_ClientId/grants/REPLACE_WITH_ResourceServerId
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "scopes": ["read:messages", "write:messages"]
}

### Revoke a client's grant to a resource server — returns 204
DELETE {{host}}/api/tenants/{{tenantId}}/clients/REPLACE_WITH_ClientId/grants/REPLACE_WITH_ResourceServerId

### List grants (first page) — scoped to the addressed tenant
GET {{host}}/api/tenants/{{tenantId}}/grants?limit=50
Accept: application/json

### List grants (next page) — replace the cursor with the previous response's continuationToken
GET {{host}}/api/tenants/{{tenantId}}/grants?limit=50&cursor=REPLACE_WITH_continuationToken
Accept: application/json

### List grants for a subject (e.g. triage one user's sessions)
GET {{host}}/api/tenants/{{tenantId}}/grants?subjectId=REPLACE_WITH_SubjectId&limit=50
Accept: application/json

### List grants for a client
GET {{host}}/api/tenants/{{tenantId}}/grants?clientId=REPLACE_WITH_ClientId&limit=50
Accept: application/json

### Get a single grant by its opaque GrantId
GET {{host}}/api/tenants/{{tenantId}}/grants/REPLACE_WITH_GrantId
Accept: application/json

### Revoke a grant (soft-revoke: sets RevokedWhen, keeps the row; idempotent) — returns 204
DELETE {{host}}/api/tenants/{{tenantId}}/grants/REPLACE_WITH_GrantId

### Bulk-revoke all of a subject's grants ("sign the user out everywhere") — returns { "revoked": N }
DELETE {{host}}/api/tenants/{{tenantId}}/grants?subjectId=REPLACE_WITH_SubjectId
Accept: application/json

### Bulk-revoke all of a client's grants ("kill a compromised client's tokens") — returns { "revoked": N }
DELETE {{host}}/api/tenants/{{tenantId}}/grants?clientId=REPLACE_WITH_ClientId
Accept: application/json

